{"schema": 1, "bench": "deser_formats", "kind": "verdict", "run": {"ts_ms": 1784040853273, "commit": "512ed5e0d247", "host": "local", "cpu": "Apple M5 Max", "cores": 18, "os": "macos/aarch64", "profile": "release"}, "variant": {"backend": "simd-json", "parses_ok": true, "licenses_ok": true, "msrv_ok": true, "faster": true}, "metrics": {}, "note": "GO \u2014 ship simd-json opt-in as the `simd` feature; serde_json stays the default. On aarch64 (M5 Max, n=9) simd-json decodes 1.41x faster than serde_json on single-document and array payloads (the Kafka-message default) and 1.16-1.26x faster on NDJSON and a flat single record. simd-json parses a mutable buffer in place, so the borrowed payload is copied into a reused thread-local buffer and the parser's own buffers are reused too; that mandatory copy is negligible (~1.1 ns/event, see the memcpy_baseline arm). Full fidelity suite passes, licenses clean (no deny.toml exception), MSRV 1.94 ok. Judged aarch64-only."}
